Spec: InstanceService

Purpose:
  Be the @ServiceInstance implementation of the shared reconcile engine: fix the service
    kind's identity literals (`service`, its finalizer, the Service package type), forward the
    macro-attached accessors and status setters to the CR model, run the service-side
    requirement evaluator @VynilPackageRequirement::check_service, build recommendations with a
    permanently empty tenant list, feed the two service metric slots, delegate @Reconciler to
    @do_reconcile/@do_cleanup, and own the controller entry pair @reconcile/@error_policy that
    ./manager.rs wires on the @ServiceInstance watch — including this kind's consumption of the
    30-second @Error::CleanupInProgress transient lane and the 5-minute counted-failure lane.

References:
  ./instance_common.sdd — @InstanceKind engine whose implementation this is: every method here
    is bound by that contract (supertraits, the seventeen required methods, the two defaults a
    service overrides, the discard-the-returned-@Self setter lanes, the verbatim
    @InstanceKind::check_requirements action pass-through, engine-owned stages and durations);
    @RecoContext, @run_with_finalizer, @do_reconcile, @do_cleanup and
    @build_base_recommendations all run from there.
  ./lib.sdd — @Reconciler implemented here per its Must; crate-root re-exported @ServiceInstance,
    @Error and @Result are the names this file imports through @crate.
  ./manager.sdd — @Context (its @metrics field is the only @Context member read here) and the
    @Controller::@run wiring that pairs this file's @instanceservice::@reconcile with
    @instanceservice::@error_policy on an @any_semantic cluster-wide watch.
  ./metrics.sdd — @Metrics::service_instance, the @count_and_measure runs increment with the
    five @LabelInstance labels, @reconcile_failure's single six-label increment and the
    @ReconcileMeasurerInstance whose @Drop observes the duration; registry prefixes there.
  /common/src/instanceservice.sdd — the @ServiceInstance CRD model this file attaches to
    (same basename as this spec, different crate: that spec owns the type, its status probe
    @ServiceInstance::have_child and the macro-attached method set; this spec owns only the
    operator-side @crate impls and entry fns co-named in ./instanceservice.rs).
  /common/src/instance_macros.sdd — the mutator contract the forwarding methods pass through
    unchanged (@ServiceInstance::get_options_digest, @ServiceInstance::set_missing_box,
    @ServiceInstance::set_missing_package, @ServiceInstance::set_missing_requirement,
    @ServiceInstance::set_missing_init_version and the server-side patch/condition semantics
    behind them).
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @VynilPackageType::Service, @VynilPackageRecommandation and the
    @VynilPackageRequirement::check_service evaluator, including its per-arm ttl seconds and the
    always-satisfied catch-all arm.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script whose @ctx receives the instance binding.

Must:
  Implement @InstanceKind for @ServiceInstance under @async_trait, overriding both engine
    defaults: @InstanceKind::init_from_version and @InstanceKind::set_missing_init_version are
    real service-lane methods, not the @None/@Ok(self) defaults.
  Fix the three identity literals: @InstanceKind::type_name answers exactly `service` (pinning,
    through the engine, the `service--<namespace>--<name>` Job name and the `package_type`
    render key), @InstanceKind::finalizer_name answers exactly `serviceinstances.vynil.solidite.fr`
    (the string kube adds on apply and removes after a @Ok cleanup), and
    @InstanceKind::package_type answers @VynilPackageType::Service (the cache-lookup type clause).
  Borrow @ServiceInstanceSpec::jukebox, @ServiceInstanceSpec::category and
    @ServiceInstanceSpec::package verbatim from @InstanceKind::spec_jukebox,
    @InstanceKind::spec_category and @InstanceKind::spec_package.
  Gate install state in @InstanceKind::current_tag: `status.tag` clone when both the status and
    the tag are present, the empty @String through @unwrap_or_default otherwise;
    @InstanceKind::init_from_version answers the @Option<@InitFrom>::version borrow — @None when
    `initFrom` or its `version` is absent.
  Forward, unmodified, the model-owned methods: @InstanceKind::have_child calls the inherent
    @ServiceInstance::have_child — Rust resolves the same-name call to the inherent probe, not
    recursively to the trait method; @InstanceKind::get_options_digest passes the `&mut self`
    receiver to the macro digest; the four setters @InstanceKind::set_missing_box,
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_package, @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement and
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_init_version call their macro counterparts on the moved copy's
    @&mut self and hand back the macro's @Result<Self> unchanged.
  Run @InstanceKind::check_requirements as an in-order scan over the requirement list with the
    moved @Client cloned per call: on the first @VynilPackageRequirement::check_service verdict
    with a false outcome, record the message via @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement on a
    clone of self (its returned @Self discarded) and return @Some(@Action::requeue(
    @tokio::time::@Duration::from_secs(ttl))) carrying that arm's ttl literal; evaluation @Err
    propagates through `?` with no condition recorded; an all-true list answers @None.
  Build @InstanceKind::build_recommendations as pure delegation plus an empty lane: the pair
    from @build_base_recommendations becomes @RecoContext::crds and
    @RecoContext::system_services, and @RecoContext::tenant_services is always @Vec::new() —
    the service kind has no tenant recommendation path even when recos would mention one.
  Bind, in @InstanceKind::set_rhai_instance, the cloned @ServiceInstance onto @Script::ctx under
    the key `instance`, so value scripts see the type registered by
    @service_rhai_register of /common/src/instanceservice.sdd.
  Wire both metric slots to @Metrics::service_instance: @InstanceKind::count_and_measure_metrics
    forwards to its @count_and_measure, @InstanceKind::record_reconcile_failure to its
    @reconcile_failure; this file adds no label of its own.
  Delegate @Reconciler wholly to the engine — @Reconciler::reconcile @Box::pins @do_reconcile
    and @Reconciler::cleanup @Box::pins @do_cleanup on `&self` with the @Arc<@Context> moved in,
    no service-specific step between.
  Instrument @reconcile `#[instrument(skip(ctx, inst), fields(trace_id))]` — the span carries a
    declared-empty `trace_id` field (the engine of ./instance_common.sdd records the same name on
    the current @Span), hides both arguments, and its body is exactly
    @Box::pin(@run_with_finalizer(inst, ctx)).await with @Ok/@Err passed through.
  Split failure handling in @error_policy on @Error::CleanupInProgress as the first test: that
    arm discards its @Job payload and answers @Action::requeue(@Duration::from_secs(30)) with no
    log line, no metric and no @tracing::@warn!; every other @Error answers
    @Action::requeue(@Duration::from_mins(5)) after the @tracing::@warn! line and exactly one
    @InstanceKind::record_reconcile_failure increment, and is matched by nothing else.

Exposes:
  @reconcile — `#[instrument] pub async fn @reconcile(inst: @Arc<@ServiceInstance>, ctx:
    @Arc<@Context>) -> @Result<@Action>`; the controller entry for the @ServiceInstance watch.
  @error_policy — `#[must_use] pub fn @error_policy(inst: @Arc<@ServiceInstance>, error:
    &@Error, ctx: @Arc<@Context>) -> @Action`; consumes both @Arcs by value, borrows the error.
  @InstanceKind for @ServiceInstance — `#[async_trait]` impl, surface and literals per Must.
  @Reconciler for @ServiceInstance — `#[async_trait]` impl delegating to @do_reconcile and
    @do_cleanup.

Accepts:
  A watch-event-carried @ServiceInstance of any shape: `spec` strings unvalidated, `status`
    @Option read opportunistically (@current_tag and @init_from_version never fail on absence),
    a requirement list of any length or emptiness (empty answers @None without a single call),
    and recos per the engine's @None-does-nothing rule.
  @error_policy accepts the @Arcs moved — nothing reads them after the metric call (the trailing
    @drop calls are explicit no-ops on already-unused owners) — and any @Error variant, the
    @Error::CleanupInProgress arm discriminating on the variant only, payload ignored.

Returns:
  @reconcile returns the @Action the engine pipeline produced for the service kind (15-minute
    requeues, ttl requeues via the pass-through, @Action::await_change() releases) and @Err the
    engine's errors — nothing here maps an @Err into an @Action.
  @error_policy returns exactly one of two requeues: @Duration::from_secs(30) on the transient
    cleanup arm, @Duration::from_mins(5) on everything else.
  @InstanceKind::check_requirements returns @None or the single short-circuit @Some requeue;
    @InstanceKind::build_recommendations a @RecoContext whose @RecoContext::tenant_services is
    empty; @InstanceKind::count_and_measure_metrics the started @ReconcileMeasurerInstance.

Raises:
  None of its own: every fallible body forwards. @InstanceKind::set_missing_box,
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_package, @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement,
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_init_version, @InstanceKind::check_requirements (through
    @VynilPackageRequirement::check_service and the condition write) and both @Reconciler
    methods propagate model, requirement or engine @Error variants — the engine variant set
    belongs to ./instance_common.sdd.
  @reconcile surfaces the same engine @Err, dominated by @Error::FinalizerError on wrapper
    failures; @error_policy is total and @Action-valued, and raises nothing in either arm.

Handles:
  A delete Job still running (@Error::CleanupInProgress) — the expected-transient 30-second
    lane: fast requeue, finalizer retained by the wrapper, runs already counted but no failure
    increment; this file is the sole consumer of that engine variant.
  Every other reconcile failure — one @tracing::@warn! naming kind, namespace and name, one
    failures-series increment on `service_instance_reconcile_failures_total`, then the 5-minute
    backoff; the warn @Debug-formats the @Option metadata, so absent-vs-present namespace reads
    `Some("apps")` vs @None inside the message (Tasks `[?]`).
  An unmet requirement — condition recorded on a discarded clone, only its ttl drives the
    requeue, later requirements unevaluated; a requirement variant the service lane's catch-all
    arm pronounces satisfied never reaches the condition write.
  A `status`-less instance during selection gates — empty tag and @None init version are plain
    answers, not errors.

Depends on:
  ./instance_common.rs — @InstanceKind, @RecoContext, @build_base_recommendations,
    @run_with_finalizer, @do_reconcile, @do_cleanup.
  ./manager.rs — @Context; read through the trait signatures, only @Context::metrics touched.
  ./metrics.rs paths — @ReconcileMeasurerInstance named in the trait surface; the
    @ReconcileMetricsServiceInstance methods run there.
  @common — @rhaihandler::@Script, @vynilpackage::@VynilPackageRecommandation,
    @VynilPackageRequirement and @VynilPackageType via the crate-root @ServiceInstance re-export.
  @kube — @Client (cloned per requirement check), @kube::runtime::controller::@Action.
  @tokio::time::@Duration, @opentelemetry::trace::@TraceId, @tracing (@instrument, @warn),
    @async_trait, @std::sync::@Arc.

Tasks:
  [ ] No test anywhere covers this file: no in-file tests module, and ./instance_common.rs tests
      exercise @TenantInstance/@SystemInstance selector lanes only. Cover from the Scenarios —
      kind literals, tag/initFrom gates, requirement short-circuit ttl, empty tenant reco list,
      both @error_policy lanes — per TTD, reusing the ./jukebox.rs fake-cluster harness style.
  [?] @error_policy warn reads `reconcile failed for ServiceInstance '{:?}.{:?}': {:?}` with
      namespace before name and @Debug on both @Option metadata fields, so shipped lines render
      `Some("apps").Some("frontend")`; and the trailing @drop(inst)/@drop(ctx) are no-ops that
      only appease move analysis. Decide whether to unwrap/flip to `name.namespace` and drop
      the dead @drop calls together.
  [?] @error_policy takes @Arcs by value while @Controller only ever needs borrows — the
      signature survives solely to feed @drop; and @reconcile's `#[instrument]` sits above its
      doc comment while the crate's other entry fns differ in order. Cosmetic-only drift:
      decide whether entry-fn style is normalized per kind spec.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a green mapped test or a decided `[?]` Task, and
  `cargo test -p operator`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`,
  `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: Kind literals pin the service identity
  Given any @ServiceInstance
  When @InstanceKind::type_name, @InstanceKind::finalizer_name and @InstanceKind::package_type
    answer
  Then they are exactly `service`, `serviceinstances.vynil.solidite.fr` and
    @VynilPackageType::Service — so the engine names the agent Job `service--<ns>--<name>` and
    the cache lookup matches only Service-type packages
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Tag and initFrom read the status gates
  Given four instances — no status, status without `tag`, installed `tag` `1.2.3`, and a fresh
    one whose `spec.initFrom.version` is `0.9.0`
  When @InstanceKind::current_tag and @InstanceKind::init_from_version run
  Then the first two answer the empty @String, the third answers `1.2.3` regardless of
    initFrom (the engine ignores the pin once installed), and @InstanceKind::init_from_version
    answers @Some(`0.9.0`) only for the fourth, @None whenever `initFrom` or its `version` is
    absent
  No mapped test exists; the sibling lanes are frozen untested by ./instance_common.sdd's
    selector-task entry, which tested tenant/system shapes only.

Scenario: First unmet service requirement short-circuits on its own ttl
  Given a requirement list whose second @VynilPackageRequirement fails @check_service with the
    ttl of its arm
  When @InstanceKind::check_requirements scans with a @Client
  Then `set missing requirement` text from the evaluator is stored via
    @InstanceKind::set_missing_requirement and the answer is @Some(@Action::requeue(ttl)) — the
    third requirement is never evaluated
  But an all-satisfied list answers @None with zero condition writes, and an evaluator @Err
    propagates with no condition written
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Recommendations keep the tenant list empty
  Given recos naming one installed CRD and one installed system service
  When @InstanceKind::build_recommendations runs with @Some recos
  Then @RecoContext carries the filtered sorted `crds` and `system_services` from
    @build_base_recommendations and an empty @Vec for @tenant_services
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: CleanupInProgress requeues fast and uncounted
  Given @error_policy met with @Error::CleanupInProgress carrying a @Job
  When it runs
  Then the answer is @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::@Duration::from_secs(30)), no @tracing::@warn!
    line is written and the failures counter does not move
  But met with any other @Error it warns once, increments
    `service_instance_reconcile_failures_total` under the six labels of ./metrics.sdd exactly
    once, and answers @Action::requeue(@tokio::time::@Duration::from_mins(5))
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Entry pair delegates with no local decision
  Given a @ServiceInstance handed to @reconcile
  When the call resolves
  Then exactly @run_with_finalizer ran — dispatching @Reconciler::reconcile, which runs
    @do_reconcile, and @Reconciler::cleanup, which runs @do_cleanup — the whole pipeline body
    belonging to ./instance_common.sdd, this file contributing only literals and forwards
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  error_policy input/output pairs: @Error::CleanupInProgress(@Job) → requeue `30` s silent;
    @Error::Other("E_X") → warn + one failure inc + requeue `5` min.
  check_requirements on [ok, fail(ttl 300)] @Ok answer: @Some(requeue `300` s).
